The truck is selling at a tiny

563
00:18:15,099 --> 00:18:16,533
fraction of that number.

564
00:18:16,713 --> 00:18:17,967
This is not an attack.

565
00:18:18,147 --> 00:18:19,157
It is arithmetic.

566
00:18:19,337 --> 00:18:22,131
A product designed and marketed for enormous

567
00:18:22,131 --> 00:18:24,608
volume is selling like a niche vehicle.

568
00:18:24,958 --> 00:18:26,293
There were other signals.

569
00:18:26,473 --> 00:18:29,801
Electrek reported that Tesla confirmed Cybertruck sales

570
00:18:29,801 --> 00:18:31,979
fell to about five thousand units in

571
00:18:31,979 --> 00:18:34,460
the second quarter of twenty twenty-five.

572
00:18:34,640 --> 00:18:36,837
In September of twenty twenty-five,

573
00:18:36,837 --> 00:18:40,102
Tesla discontinued the cheapest Cybertruck trim only

574
00:18:40,102 --> 00:18:41,734
months after launching it.

575
00:18:41,914 --> 00:18:43,475
And in the final quarter,

576
00:18:43,475 --> 00:18:46,285
the Autopian reported that companies owned by

577
00:18:46,285 --> 00:18:48,470
Elon Musk bought nearly one in five

578
00:18:48,470 --> 00:18:50,343
of the Cybertrucks Tesla sold.

579
00:18:50,693 --> 00:18:52,447
Here is the twist that keeps the

580
00:18:52,447 --> 00:18:54,477
Cybertruck on this list for the right

581
00:18:54,477 --> 00:18:54,861
reason.

582
00:18:55,041 --> 00:18:56,832
The sales gap is not a verdict

583
00:18:56,832 --> 00:18:57,966
on the engineering.

584
00:18:58,146 --> 00:19:00,384
It is the gap between a forecast

585
00:19:00,384 --> 00:19:01,293
and a market.

586
00:19:01,473 --> 00:19:02,918
A product can be famous,

587
00:19:02,918 --> 00:19:05,387
discussed everywhere, and still sell to a

588
00:19:05,387 --> 00:19:08,218
much smaller audience than its maker predicted.

589
00:19:08,398 --> 00:19:10,128
Fame sells headlines.

590
00:19:10,308 --> 00:19:12,351
It does not automatically sell trucks.

591
00:19:12,702 --> 00:19:13,379
To be fair,

592
00:19:13,379 --> 00:19:16,025
the Cybertruck still has something Ford and

593
00:19:16,025 --> 00:19:17,195
Ram could not keep.

594
00:19:17,375 --> 00:19:18,958
It is still in production,

595
00:19:18,958 --> 00:19:21,090
and Tesla has not announced an end.

596
00:19:21,270 --> 00:19:23,761
The EV pickup market is smaller than

597
00:19:23,761 --> 00:19:27,083
anyone predicted, but the Cybertruck can survive

598
00:19:27,083 --> 00:19:28,398
on a smaller scale.

599
00:19:28,578 --> 00:19:30,970
Pickup Truck Talk reports that the Model

600
00:19:30,970 --> 00:19:33,003
3 and Model Y made up ninety-seven

601
00:19:33,003 --> 00:19:34,557
percent of Tesla's volume.

602
00:19:34,737 --> 00:19:36,652
The company does not depend on the

603
00:19:36,652 --> 00:19:36,990
truck.

604
00:19:37,170 --> 00:19:39,327
That is a very different position from

605
00:19:39,327 --> 00:19:41,256
a company that needed its truck to

606
00:19:41,256 --> 00:19:41,767
be a hit.

607
00:19:42,118 --> 00:19:44,131
So what is the pattern across all

608
00:19:44,131 --> 00:19:44,498
seven?

609
00:19:44,678 --> 00:19:46,531
Four of them are electric trucks,

610
00:19:46,531 --> 00:19:47,766
or were planned to be.

611
00:19:47,946 --> 00:19:50,651
One was a Japanese brand's full-size truck

612
00:19:50,651 --> 00:19:52,648
that never found enough buyers.

613
00:19:52,828 --> 00:19:55,246
One was a medium-duty truck that depended

614
00:19:55,246 --> 00:19:57,251
on a partner who sold the factory.

615
00:19:57,431 --> 00:20:00,294
One is a small Korean-brand pickup beaten

616
00:20:00,294 --> 00:20:02,389
six to one by a cheaper rival.

617
00:20:02,569 --> 00:20:04,484
Different problems, same lesson.

618
00:20:04,664 --> 00:20:06,650
A truck is not just a vehicle.

619
00:20:06,830 --> 00:20:08,479
It is a bet on a factory,

620
00:20:08,479 --> 00:20:09,864
a partner, a battery,

621
00:20:09,864 --> 00:20:10,656
and a buyer,

622
00:20:10,656 --> 00:20:12,635
and any one of them can break.

623
00:20:12,984 --> 00:20:14,196
That matters for you,

624
00:20:14,196 --> 00:20:16,042
because buying a truck is a long

625
00:20:16,042 --> 00:20:16,676
commitment.

626
00:20:16,856 --> 00:20:18,448
Here is what to check before you

627
00:20:18,448 --> 00:20:19,840
sign in twenty twenty-seven.

628
00:20:20,020 --> 00:20:21,953
First, look at the sales trend of

629
00:20:21,953 --> 00:20:22,890
the exact model,

630
00:20:22,890 --> 00:20:24,002
not just the brand.

631
00:20:24,182 --> 00:20:26,631
A truck whose sales are falling year

632
00:20:26,631 --> 00:20:28,808
after year is a warning sign for

633
00:20:28,808 --> 00:20:30,916
resale value and parts support.

634
00:20:31,096 --> 00:20:33,364
Second, find out who actually builds it,

635
00:20:33,364 --> 00:20:35,291
and whether a partner or a factory

636
00:20:35,291 --> 00:20:36,425
change could end it.

637
00:20:36,776 --> 00:20:39,170
Third, ask what the warranty and service

638
00:20:39,170 --> 00:20:40,966
plan look like if the model is

639
00:20:40,966 --> 00:20:41,745
discontinued.

640
00:20:41,925 --> 00:20:44,021
A warranty normally stays valid on a

641
00:20:44,021 --> 00:20:46,584
discontinued model, but get that in writing,

642
00:20:46,584 --> 00:20:49,146
because parts and dealer attention can fade.

643
00:20:49,326 --> 00:20:51,088
Fourth, compare the full cost,

644
00:20:51,088 --> 00:20:52,321
not just the sticker.

645
00:20:52,501 --> 00:20:55,350
Charging, fuel, insurance and what the truck

646
00:20:55,350 --> 00:20:57,356
will be worth in five years all

647
00:20:57,356 --> 00:20:58,910
belong on the same page.

648
00:20:59,090 --> 00:21:01,006
A cheap truck nobody wants can be

649
00:21:01,006 --> 00:21:03,212
the most expensive one you ever owned.

